{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-033", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Germany reduces solar feed-in tariffs by 1%", "content": "<p>Fixed feed-in tariffs for solar systems under the partial feed-in model will now range from €0.0544 ($0.063)/kWh to €0.0770/kWh, while systems operating under the full feed-in model will receive between €0.1024/kWh and €0.1222/kWh.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/03/germany-reduces-solar-feed-in-tariffs-by-1/\">Germany reduces solar feed-in tariffs by 1%</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/03/germany-reduces-solar-feed-in-tariffs-by-1/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-034", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Peruvian researchers develop foldable solar panels for naval, mining applications", "content": "<p>The technology uses a pattern inspired by Japanese origami to fold the photovoltaic panels in a single movement. A prototype weighs around 6 kg and can be transported in a suitcase.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/03/peruvian-researchers-develop-foldable-solar-panels-for-naval-mining-applications/\">Peruvian researchers develop foldable solar panels for naval, mining applications</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/03/peruvian-researchers-develop-foldable-solar-panels-for-naval-mining-applications/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-03-035", "date": "2026-08-03", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Scientists develop perovskite-organic tandem solar cell with enhanced reverse-bias stability", "content": "<p>Researchers from the Hong Kong Polytechnic University have developed a perovskite–organic tandem solar cell with enhanced reverse-bias stability, addressing a key reliability challenge in thin-film PV technologies. The device achieved strong resistance to voltage-induced damage by suppressing leakage pathways and defects, retaining more than 90% of its initial efficiency under severe reverse-bias stress.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/03/scientists-develop-perovs", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/03/scientists-develop-perovskite-organic-tandem-solar-cell-with-enhanced-reverse-bias-stability/", "type": "rss"}]}
